  :adr/cljs-backend
  {:where "kotoba-lang/compiler, not kotoba-lang/kotoba -- compiler/ already
           has the frontend->HIR->KIR->backend separation a new backend
           needs; kotoba/'s single-pass compile-wasm-expr does not."
   :new-targets ["cljs-kotoba-v1 (generic)" "cljs-node-kotoba-v1" "cljs-browser-kotoba-v1"]
   :design
   ["KIR's :functions bodies are already a small closed Lisp (let/if/
     cap-call/pair-family/arithmetic/comparison/named calls) -- 1:1
     data->data rewrite to cljs s-expressions, no byte assembly needed"
    "pair/pair-first/pair-second become plain 2-element vectors + nth
     (cljs already has real heap-allocated persistent data structures) --
     simpler than wasm32/x86_64/aarch64's hand-rolled linear-memory heap"
    "KIR's if treats exactly 0 as false (cljs/clj's own if treats 0 as
     truthy) -- every if wraps its test as (if (zero? test) else then)"
    "KIR's comparison ops return integer 1/0, not boolean -- every
     comparison wraps as (if (cljs-op ...) 1 0) to compose with the above"
    "fuel: WASM's module-global, never-replenished 256-call counter
     reproduced via a defonce atom -- same global-depletion semantics,
     not 256-per-top-level-call"
    "cap-call rejected at emit time (no cljs-side host-import wiring yet)
     -- explicit compile error, not a silent stub"
    "i64 wraparound (KIR's normative 2's-complement overflow semantics) is
     NOT reproduced -- plain cljs +/-/* auto-promote to bignum. Documented,
     unaddressed gap: every known safe-kotoba-subset program stays well
     inside JS's 53-bit safe-integer range, so unreachable in practice, but
     real for a hypothetical overflow-dependent program"]
   :real-bug-found-and-fixed
   {:bug "KIR's :functions order does not guarantee a synthesized loop/recur
          helper is defined before the defn that calls it (the originating
          defn is listed first, its own loop-helpers appended after, per
          ADR-2607150000's addendum 4) -- plain defn forms do not forward-
          hoist across a file in cljs OR JVM Clojure, unlike WASM/native
          backends which resolve calls through a pre-built function-index
          table before any body is assembled"
    :symptom "confirmed live via REAL nbb execution (not just a hypothesis):
              'Unable to resolve symbol: __kotoba_loop_1', identical failure
              under plain JVM eval of the same emitted text"
    :fix "emit a (declare fn1 fn2 ...) of every KIR function name ahead of
          any defn -- handles arbitrary call order/mutual recursion"}
   :verification
   {:real-nbb-execution
    "hand-verified before committing: nbb (ClojureScript-on-Node) actually
     required and called the emitted namespace for every scenario (plain
     arithmetic, pair round-trip, if-0-is-false, multi-defn calls,
     loop/recur via the frontend's own desugar, quot-by-zero throwing,
     the global fuel-depletion property across 256+ calls) -- this is what
     caught the forward-reference bug above"
    :committed-tests
    "10 new deftest in test/kotoba/compiler/backend_cljs_test.clj, evaling
     emitted source under PLAIN JVM CLOJURE (legitimate here specifically
     because nothing backend.cljs ever emits is cljs-specific -- defn/let/
     if/vector/nth/atom/swap!/throw/ex-info/a namespaced map literal are
     valid, identical Clojure AND ClojureScript). Matches this compiler's
     own established convention of NOT depending on an external runtime
     (Chicory for wasm) in its committed suite."
    :full-suite "clojure -M:test: 131 tests / 2786 assertions (121 pre-
                 existing + 10 new), 0 failures/errors. :cljs-kotoba-v1
                 added to compiler/targets (compatibility-targets), so
                 every existing cross-backend consistency test now also
