  :adr/cap-call-support-2026-07-14
  {:summary "Closed the cap-call gap documented at initial landing: the
             cljs backend previously rejected any KIR function body using
             cap-call at emit time (no cljs-side host-import wiring). Now
             emits an exported set-cap-dispatch! (a fn [cap-id value] ->
             i64) the host installs before calling main -- this backend's
             equivalent of WASM's kotoba:cap host import."
   :design
   ["defonce kotoba$cap-dispatch atom, defaults to nil"
    "set-cap-dispatch! (public defn) installs the host's dispatch fn"
    "kotoba$cap-call (private) looks up the dispatcher; throws
     :capability-denied if none installed -- fail-closed, matching
     kotoba-lang/kotoba's own has-capability-fn convention (no policy
     grants nothing) rather than defaulting to permissive"
    "cap-id is always a literal integer in [0,255] (validated by
     frontend.clj's validate-expr, never itself an expression) -- passes
     through lower-expr unchanged, only the value argument recurses"]
   :verification
   {:real-nbb-execution "hand-verified before committing: both the
                         no-dispatcher-denies-fail-closed case and the
                         dispatcher-installed-dispatches-correctly case,
                         via real nbb (ClojureScript-on-Node) execution"
    :committed-tests "the old cap-call-is-rejected-at-emit-time test
                       replaced with 2 new deftest: cap-call-with-no-
                       dispatcher-installed-is-denied-fail-closed and
                       cap-call-dispatches-to-the-installed-host-function"
    :full-suite "clojure -M:test: 142 tests / 2842 assertions, 0 failures"}
