  :adr/kotoba-cljs-backend-2026-07-15
  {:summary "Addressed (in narrowed form) the follow-up gap this same ADR's
             :adr/decision-not-made had flagged: kotoba-lang/kotoba itself
             gained its own compile-cljs-expr / cljs-source ClojureScript
             backend in src/kotoba/runtime.clj, mirroring compiler/'s
             backend/cljs.clj but scoped to only the ops the kototama/
             cloud-itonami narrow-slice governor ports actually use
             (arithmetic, comparison, and/or/not/zero?/pos?/neg?/inc/dec,
             pair, map-literal get/assoc) -- NOT compile-wasm-expr's full
             2000+-line op surface (i64/f32/bitwise/string/memory/capability
             explicitly rejected at compile time via a closed
             cljs-unsupported-ops set)."
   :architectural-simplifications
   ["no locals index-bookkeeping needed at all: compile-wasm-expr threads a
     symbol->numeric-index locals map because WASM locals need indices;
     cljs's own let/defn bind symbolic names natively so compile-cljs-expr
     carries no locals context whatsoever"
    "pair/pair-first/pair-second lower to plain vectors + nth (cljs has real
     persistent data structures; no need for WASM's hand-rolled pair
     encoding)"
    "no memory-based host ABI: kotoba wasm's 0-arity main constraint (forcing
     real args through mem-i32-at reads) does not exist for a cljs target --
     defns keep their real declared parameters. Honest scope limit: existing
     mem-i32-at-based .kotoba sources (e.g. the governor ports) do NOT
     compile unchanged to this new target."]
