  :adr/compiler-cli-cljs-output-bug-fixed-2026-07-15
  {:summary "While auditing kotoba-lang/compiler's own CLI (kotoba.compiler.
             cli) for the same emit-CLI asymmetry addendum 7 fixed in
             kotoba-lang/kotoba, discovered `compile --target cljs-kotoba-v1`
             was ALREADY reachable from the CLI (compile-source already had
             a (= backend :cljs-kotoba-v1) branch returning {:format :cljs/v1
             ... :source \"...\"}) but silently BROKEN: the CLI's `compile`
             command branched only on :wasm/v1 vs everything-else, and
             unconditionally wrote (:artifact result) via write-edn! for the
             else branch. A :cljs/v1 result has no :artifact key -- so this
             wrote the literal text \"nil\" to --output while still
             reporting {:ok true ...}. Reproduced live BEFORE fixing:
             `compile demo.kotoba --target cljs-kotoba-v1 --output demo.cljs
             && cat demo.cljs` printed exactly `nil`. Worse than a crash --
             it silently succeeds while producing garbage, unlike kotoba/'s
             own :cljs/emit-unsupported which at least surfaces as ok?=false."
   :also-fixed "the default --output extension logic only distinguished
                :wasm execution (.wasm) from everything else (.kexe) -- a
                cljs target with no explicit --output additionally got the
                wrong .kexe extension on top of the wrong (nil) content"
   :fix
